<section class="section-vnv section-white">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center section-heading" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
            <span class="vnv-badge">Common Questions</span>
            <h2>Before You Call, You Might Be <span class="text-vnv">Wondering...</span></h2>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-wrap">
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>How far in advance should we book a planner?</h4>
                <p>Ideally 6–12 months out for weddings, especially during peak season (November–May). Corporate and social events can often work with less notice — call us and we'll tell you honestly if your timeline works.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>We already booked a few vendors — can we still get a planner?</h4>
                <p>Yes. Most clients come to us with at least one vendor already booked. Your planner works with what you have and fills in the gaps from there.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>Can we upgrade our package later?</h4>
                <p>Yes. Many clients start with Basic and add hours or move up to Gold or Premium as the event gets closer and more decisions come up.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>Is the event-day coordinator always Mary?</h4>
                <p>Not always. Mary leads the planning process for every client, but your event-day coordinator is whoever on our team is the best fit for your specific event and date.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

